<section class="card">
  <h2>1. Developer options</h2>
  <p>Settings → About tablet → Software information → tap <b>Build number</b> 7 times. Then in Developer options turn on <b>USB debugging</b> and <b>Wireless debugging</b>.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <button data-open="dev-settings">Open Developer options</button>
    <button data-open="wireless-debugging">Open Wireless debugging</button>
  </div>
  <p class="status" id="s-adbd"></p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>2. Pair (one time)</h2>
  <p>In <b>Wireless debugging</b> tap <b>Pair device with pairing code</b>, note the <b>6-digit code</b>, switch back here quickly and enter it. The pairing port is found automatically (the dialog keeps listening for a while in the background). Split-screen works too.</p>
  <form id="pairform" class="row wrap">
    <label>Pairing code <input id="pair-code" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" placeholder="6 digits" required autocomplete="one-time-code"></label>
    <label>Pairing port (optional) <input id="pair-port" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" placeholder="auto"></label>
    <button class="primary">Pair</button>
  </form>
  <p class="status" id="s-pair"></p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>3. Connect</h2>
  <p>The connect port is found automatically (it changes after every reboot). If auto-detect fails, read the <b>IP address &amp; Port</b> shown on the Wireless debugging screen and enter just the port.</p>
  <form id="connform" class="row wrap">
    <button id="btn-auto2" class="primary" type="button">Auto connect</button>
    <label>or port <input id="conn-port" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" placeholder="e.g. 39321"></label>
    <button type="submit">Connect</button>
  </form>
  <p class="status" id="s-conn"></p>
  <pre id="log" class="log" hidden></pre>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2>4. Install as an app</h2>
  <p>In this browser's menu choose <b>Add to Home screen</b> / <b>Install app</b>. Start the backend any time from Termux with <code>inspect</code> (or the Termux:Widget shortcut).</p>
  <p class="hint">Trouble? Wireless debugging switches itself off on some firmware after a reboot. Toggle it on, then tap Auto connect.</p>
</section>
